      "worked": "<strong>Trace this loop step by step:</strong><br><code>int sum = 0, i;</code><br><code>for (i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) { sum = sum + i; }</code><br><br><strong>Before the loop:</strong> sum = 0, i is not set yet<br><strong>Initialisation:</strong> i = 1 (happens once only)<br><br><strong>Pass 1:</strong> condition 1 &lt;= 5 is TRUE &rarr; sum = 0 + 1 = <strong>1</strong> &rarr; update i++ makes i = 2<br><strong>Pass 2:</strong> condition 2 &lt;= 5 is TRUE &rarr; sum = 1 + 2 = <strong>3</strong> &rarr; i becomes 3<br><strong>Pass 3:</strong> condition 3 &lt;= 5 is TRUE &rarr; sum = 3 + 3 = <strong>6</strong> &rarr; i becomes 4<br><strong>Pass 4:</strong> condition 4 &lt;= 5 is TRUE &rarr; sum = 6 + 4 = <strong>10</strong> &rarr; i becomes 5<br><strong>Pass 5:</strong> condition 5 &lt;= 5 is TRUE &rarr; sum = 10 + 5 = <strong>15</strong> &rarr; i becomes 6<br><strong>Pass 6:</strong> condition 6 &lt;= 5 is FALSE &rarr; loop ends immediately, body does NOT run<br><br><strong>Final answer: sum = 15, and i = 6 after the loop (not 5).</strong><br>Notice the body ran 5 times but the condition was tested 6 times — the last test is the one that stops it.",
